---
/**
 * The site's section nav, in `cs-page`'s `subheader` slot.
 *
 * Upstream carries the same band below its header, and it is what lets its browse page drop the sidebar
 * without losing every way out of the page. Ours needed it for the same reason once `/components` became
 * `template: splash`.
 *
 * **Measured against theirs rather than approximated.** Their band is two elements — a `page-subheader`
 * carrying the surface, a bottom rule and `8px 0` of padding, wrapping a capped, centred
 * `subheader content-container` on `0 40px` — which is the split below. Ours lands on the same numbers
 * because `cs-page` already gives a slotted subheader `8px` of block padding and `--content-padding-inline`
 * is 40px.
 *
 * The items are **buttons, not styled anchors**: upstream uses `wa-button appearance="plain" size="s"` with
 * an `href`, and the design skill's first rung says to reach for the component when the markup starts to
 * look like one. That is also where the band's height comes from — a small button is 38px, so the band needs
 * no height of its own — and it brings a hit area, a radius and a hover state that a bare link would each
 * have needed a rule for. The gap is `2xs` for the same reason: the spacing lives inside the buttons as
 * `0 14px` of padding, so the gap between them is only 4px.
 *
 * `subheader` is a documented slot and part, and `cs-page` measures it into `--subheader-height`, which
 * `--scroll-margin-top` already sums with the header — so anchors keep landing correctly with no arithmetic
 * here.
 *
 * `aria-current="page"` marks the section. Upstream uses `class="current"` and no ARIA, which is a gap on
 * their side; the attribute is both the hook the styling hangs off and the thing a screen reader reads.
 *
 * `slot="subheader"` sits on the `<div>` here rather than on `<Subheader slot="subheader" />` at the use
 * site. An Astro component is not an element, so the attribute has nowhere to land there and the band
 * renders as default-slot content instead — inside `main`, with none of `cs-page`'s
 * `::slotted([slot='subheader'])` styling, and `--subheader-height` measuring 0 while the links still
 * paint. `PageFrame.astro`'s own `<header>` and `<aside>` carry their slot attributes for the same reason.
 */
import { sectionFor, siteSections } from '../site-sections.js';

const current = sectionFor(Astro.url.pathname);
---

<div class="site-subheader" slot="subheader">
  <nav class="site-subheader-inner cs-cluster cs-gap-2xs cs-flex-nowrap" aria-label="Sections">
    {
      siteSections.map((section) => (
        <cs-button
          class="site-subheader-link"
          appearance="plain"
          size="s"
          href={section.link}
          aria-current={section === current ? 'page' : undefined}
        >
          {section.label}
        </cs-button>
      ))
    }
  </nav>
</div>
